You can configure some aspects of the GitHub Actions-based CI on a
per-repository basis by setting "variables" and "secrets" from with the
GitHub web interface. These can be found at:

  https://github.com/<user>/git/settings/secrets/actions

The following variables can be used:

 - CI_BRANCHES

   The CI workflow runs on pull request updates (including drafts), and
   on pushes to the integration and release branches listed in the
   workflow, and on tag pushes. A non-empty CI_BRANCHES further
   restricts these runs by ref name. Use shortened names separated by spaces
   (e.g., "pwrgit", "v2.56.0", or "31/merge").
